title: Tutorial_Memory_Introduction
---
// Shu Wen: the story opening lives in Assets/Marcus/Scripts/Story/Tutorial/Tutorial.yarn.
// This node starts on the first Memory World visit of a new game.
// Mother's Study dialogue is a separate node below; do not add memory_complete to this opening node.
<<detour Tutorial>>
//You have entered the Memory World. Echoes of the past can help restore what has been lost. #line:tutorial_intro_001
//Move with WASD or the arrow keys. Hold E near the cabinet key to reveal its Echo. #line:tutorial_intro_002
//Release E, then hold E again to capture the Echo. Hold 1 near the locked cabinet to replay it. #line:tutorial_intro_003
//Collect the memory fragments, then open the Manual with R to reconstruct the memory. Your objective will guide you. #line:tutorial_intro_004
===

title: Tutorial_Mother_Message
---
// Starts after restoring and entering the Study. Edit Mother's approved dialogue here.
Father: You're here, Jade. 
Mother: Hello, Jade. #line:tutorial_mother_001
<<portrait Character_Image JadeSmile_0>>
Jade: Father and Mother? Is it really you?
<<portrait Character_Image none>>
Mother: There is so much that we want to tell you, my dear. But we don't have much time.
Father: Our family have been memory recorders for generations.
Mother: We see, we preserve, we remember.
Father: If you had reached here, it means you've met Mem and completed the training.
Mem: Master, I am confident that Jade will succeed you brilliantly
Father: Haha! I am sure that my daughter will do well. After all, she takes after me. 
Mother: Look at him being proud again. Well, Jade, there's still much for you to learn.
Father: Now, now. We should get to the important part.
Father: It's time for the succession.
Father: My daughter, Jade, are you ready?
-> I am not ready.
    Mother: Don't worry, my dear. It is alright to feel this way.
    Mother: No one starts a journey knowing everything.
    Mother: You just need to find the courage to take the first step, and you will know.
    -> ... I will try my best.
-> I am ready.
    Father: I knew you would be.
Father: That's my girl. Remember to say strong despite the hurdles ahead.
Father: We will learn, grow and conquer them.
Father: Now, then. As the 17th successor, I hereby declare you the 18th successor of the memory shop.
Father: Mem, I will now entrust her with you. Please guide her well.
Mem: I understand, Master. I shall guide her to the best of my ability.
Father: Mem, Jade is now your master.
Mother: All the best, Jade.

Jade: Wait! I still have many things to ask you about.
Jade: Why did you leave me? Where did you go? What happened?
Father: We wish we could stay longer.
Mother: ...You will need to discover it in your own time.
Jade: Please don't go.
Mother: Remember, my dear... Even if we are not here, we love you deeply from our heart...
Father: You are always our pride and joy...
<<memory_complete>>
===

title: Recorder
---

Mother: The memory machine is an asset that is passed down in our family for generations.

<<cameraShift studyFragmentTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: Next, collect the fragment near the Study.
Mem: Hold E beside that glowing fragment to collect it.
<<cameraReturn>>

===

title: Recorder_Study_Collected
---
// The Study fragment was collected first. The controller queues the appropriate next step.
Mum: The memory machine is an asset that is passed down in our family for generations.

===

title: FamilyPhoto
---
<<portrait Character_Image JadeSmile_0>>
Jade: It’s a photo of a family. That child… It looks like me when I was young.
 
Jade: Then are those two my parents?
<<portrait Character_Image none>>
Mem: You have succeeded in collecting your first memory fragment. Congratulations.

<<cameraShift EchoTarget 0.75>>
Mem: There is still echoes at the next room. Let's go.
 
===


title: FogLocked
---
Mem: This area has not been reconstructed yet.

Mem: Find fragments and clues to reconstruct it.

===

title: Tutorial_Cabinet_Locked
---
Mem: Rule 1 of the memory world: You cannot touch or change remembered objects in the Memory World. 
Mem: The cabinet is locked. To do so we will need a Memory Echo which remember an action of the past.
Mem: So to open the cabinet, we will need to collect the corresponding Memory Echo before we can open it.
<<cameraShift keyEchoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: Look at the glowing key above the fridge. It is a Memory Echo.
Mem: Hold E near the key to reveal its Echo. Release E, then hold E again to capture it.
<<cameraReturn>>
===

title: Tutorial_Key_Echo_Captured
---
Mem: You have captured the Cabinet Key Echo. It is now stored in slot 1.
<<cameraShift cabinetEchoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: Memory Echoes are actions remembered by this world. Replaying the Key Echo will repeat the action of unlocking the cabinet.
Mem: Stand beside the locked cabinet and hold 1 to replay the Echo.
<<cameraReturn>>
===

title: Tutorial_Cabinet_Opened
---
<<cameraShift cabinetEchoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
The cabinet is open. A recorder fragment was hidden inside.
Mem: Hold E beside the recorder to collect its memory fragment.
<<cameraReturn>>
===

title: Tutorial_Reconstruction_Ready
---
Mem: You have collected all three memory fragments. It is time to reconstruct the memory.
Mem: Open the Manual with R and select Reconstruction.
Mem: Drag the fragments into the blanks and Reconstruct. The memory will reveal the Study.
===

title: Tutorial_Find_Mother_Fragment
---
<<cameraShift photoTarget>>
<<cameraKeep>>
Mem: There is still one fragment remaining: the family photo.
Mem: Hold E beside it to collect the Mother fragment. Then we can reconstruct the memory.
<<cameraReturn>>
===
